typhoon patch on felucca-bsp: the USB audio streams presented, chosen at run time (chip/usb.c usb_audio_switch)
SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 (a change to felucca-bsp's MPL-2.0 file)

What: the device presents both audio streams, the recording (EP4 IN) alone, the playback (EP4 OUT) alone, or
neither (MIDI only), chosen at run time: usb_audio_switch, at boot before usb_start or later (a change while
attached drops off the bus and usb_retry attaches again within a second, as usb_cdc_switch does). Each layout has
its own bcdDevice low byte, as builds with other streams have, so a host that keeps what it learnt of a device
reads it afresh. The interface numbers follow (the playback's is 2 when there is no recording); requests for a
stream not presented stall. The console, when presented, keeps both (the layout as built). The layout as built is
the default, byte for byte.
Why: a player keeps the FM-1's audio off the computer unless wanted (Windows makes a new audio device its default).
Applies to: felucca-bsp 2cd696a (as fm1-base 934e40d pins it in base/bsp).
Upstream: not offered yet (hugelton/felucca-bsp).

